{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeJucysMurphyElements"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_adjacent_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_adjacent_one","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L245-L261","doc":"**Adjacent commutativity at `i = 1`: `L₂L₃ = L₃L₂`.**\n\nThe first genuine instance of the case the exchange relations could not reach.  Both products are\nthe full twist, approached from opposite sides — `L₂L₃ = (σ₀σ₁)³` (`jmRaw_prod_three`) and\n`L₃L₂ = (σ₁σ₀)³` (`jmRaw_two_mul_one`) — and `fullTwist3_symm` identifies those.\n\n**This is one instance, not the general theorem.**  It works because at `i = 1` both products are\n*the whole* full twist of `B₃`, so the half-twist symmetry closes it; for `i ≥ 2` the products are\nproper sub-words and that argument does not apply.  General adjacent commutativity remains open\n(bean `qou-u9o1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_two_mul_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_two_mul_one","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L235-L243","doc":"`L₃L₂ = (σ₁σ₀)³` — the mirror of `jmRaw_prod_three`, by one braid application. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist3_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist3_symm","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L222-L233","doc":"**`(σ₀σ₁)³ = (σ₁σ₀)³`** — both are `Δ·Δ` for the half-twist `Δ = σ₀σ₁σ₀ = σ₁σ₀σ₁`.\n\n`(σ₀σ₁)³` groups as `(σ₀σ₁σ₀)(σ₁σ₀σ₁)` and `(σ₁σ₀)³` as `(σ₁σ₀σ₁)(σ₀σ₁σ₀)`; the braid relation\nturns each factor into the other, so both collapse to the same square. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_hook","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_hook","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L194-L214","doc":"**The hook-word form**: `L_k = (σ_{k−1}⋯σ₁) σ₀² (σ₁⋯σ_{k−1})` for `k ≥ 1`.\n\nA palindrome around `σ₀²`.  Proved by induction directly on the recursion\n`L_{k+1} = σ_k L_k σ_k`, which appends `σ_k` to each side — so the two products grow in step and\nthe centre never moves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.ascProd_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.ascProd_succ","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L188-L192","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.descProd_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.descProd_succ","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L182-L186","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.ascProd_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.ascProd_one","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L180-L180","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.descProd_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.descProd_one","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L179-L179","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.ascProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.ascProd","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L173-L177","doc":"Ascending product `σ₁ ⋯ σ_{k−1}`, empty for `k ≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.descProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.descProd","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L167-L171","doc":"Descending product `σ_{k−1} σ_{k−2} ⋯ σ₁`, empty for `k ≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_sigma_far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_sigma_far","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L128-L154","doc":"**`σⱼ` commutes with `Lᵢ` whenever `j > i`** (strictly).\n\n`jmRaw H i` is a word in `σ₀ … σ_{i−1}`, so `j > i` puts `σⱼ` at distance `≥ 2` from every letter\nand the presentation's `far` relation applies at each one.  Induction on `i`.\n\n**The strictness is not a technicality.**  At `j = i` the generator `σᵢ` is *adjacent* to the\noutermost letter of `L_{i+1}`, `far` does not apply, and that boundary case is exactly the open\nadjacent-commutativity problem this file could not close.  An earlier draft of this theorem stated\n`i ≤ j` and was mathematically wrong for that reason; the Lean caught it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_mul_jm_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_mul_jm_prod","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L104-L124","doc":"**`σᵢ (Lᵢ L_{i+1}) = (L_{i+1} Lᵢ) σᵢ`.**\n\nNote the **order swap** on the right: this is not yet \"σᵢ commutes with the product\".  It becomes\nthat precisely when `Lᵢ` and `L_{i+1}` commute — which is the open problem, so this identity must\nnot be quoted as commutation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_add","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L85-L102","doc":"**`σᵢ` commutes with `Lᵢ + L_{i+1}`.**\n\nThe two exchange relations carry the *same* `h·L_{i+1}` term, so it cancels in the sum:\n\n    σᵢ(Lᵢ + L_{i+1}) = σᵢLᵢ + (h·L_{i+1} + Lᵢσᵢ)\n                     = (L_{i+1}σᵢ − h·L_{i+1}) + h·L_{i+1} + Lᵢσᵢ\n                     = (Lᵢ + L_{i+1})σᵢ.\n\nThis is the classical fact that `σᵢ` commutes with the *symmetric functions* of the adjacent JM\npair.  It holds at **every** `i` — the first general commutation statement in this corpus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jm_succ_mul_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jm_succ_mul_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L74-L81","doc":"**`L_{i+1} σᵢ = h L_{i+1} + σᵢ Lᵢ`** — the mirror relation, from the trailing `σᵢ·σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_mul_jm_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_mul_jm_succ","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeJucysMurphyCommutation.lean#L64-L72","doc":"**`σᵢ L_{i+1} = h L_{i+1} + Lᵢ σᵢ`**, with `h = q − q⁻¹`.  One application of the Hecke\nrelation `σᵢ² = hσᵢ + 1` to the leading `σᵢ·σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}